kb/events_buffer.md:61:- [[REDACTED]T06:40:50Z] quant-skeptic/verification — ✅ [REDACTED]VERIFY: GDKHQ code hoa D1-D3 XONG: cong mot-he-quy-chieu cho tang DAT LENH (commit e39aafb + a3dc7aff), 53/53 selfcheck gom 2 ca chung minh nguoc tu artifact that, hoi quy 61/61 plan 0 lenh doi gia tri — CHUA ap cho plan that nao: {"finding_topic": "GDKHQ code hoa D1-D3 XONG: cong mot-he-quy-chieu cho tang DAT LENH (commit e39aafb + a3dc7aff), 53/53 selfcheck gom 2 ca chung minh nguoc tu artifact that, hoi quy 61/61 plan 0 lenh doi gia tri — CHUA ap cho plan that nao", "verdict": "[REDACTED]D", "confidence": "high", "checks": {"look_ahead_leak": "pass — grepped price_frame.py, exdate_gate.py, merge_park_orders.py, paper_main_probe_plan.py, lag_entry_anchor.py for profit_2W/1M/2M/3M, O1W..O2Y, *_center_* — zero hits. Mechanism only forces same-session reference-frame consistency for order sizing (T+0/T+1 execution), not a forward-looking signal.", "oos_robustness": "na — this is an execution-layer correctness fix (order sizing frame consistency), not an alpha/backtest claim. No IS/OOS split applies.", "panel_curation_bias": "na — universe is 'every ticker in a real held plan', not a curated performance panel; no return claim is being made.", "reproducibility_selfcheck": "pass — independently reran exdate_price_frame_selfcheck.py: got exactly 53 '  PASS' test lines + 1 summary line, matching the 53/53 claim exactly, identical output under `env -u TZ`, `TZ=UTC`, `TZ=America/New_York`. Independently reran replay_plans_regression.py live against BigQuery (sourced wc_env.sh myself, bq CLI): 65 plans/40 tickers/[REDACTED]→08-17, 61/61 no-event plans untouched, exactly 4 event-touched plans ([REDACTED] 08-11, [REDACTED] 08-11, main 07-09, main 08-11) — matches claim verbatim, exit 0. Also independently reran 11 of the cited 19 scope-map selfchecks (rule_a_ref_guard 54/54, rule_a_ceiling all-pass, dcf_check, dcf_selector, capit_lever, merge_park_orders all-pass, verify_account_snapshot_corp_action 12/12, corp_action 73/73, filter_lag_entry_window 52/52, corp_action_daily 178/178, discretionary_accumulation 33/33, ghost_order all-pass) — zero regressions found.", "param_overfit": "pass — no metric-tuned parameters. REF_PRICE_EXDATE_TOL=1% and EX_WINDOW_DAYS=4 calendar days are derived from measured min/median deviation (0.8% min / 5.46% median across 22 ticker-days) and reuse the existing RULE_A_REF_TOL_DEFAULT constant, not swept against a backtest metric.", "capacity_adv_realism": "na — execution-correctness bug affecting real order sizing on GDKHQ days regardless of ADV; not an alpha/capacity claim.", "arithmetic_mechanism": "pass — independently verified on live BQ: (1) corp_action_lib event_status trap reproduced exactly (executed_only=True→0 rows, pricing_events→5 rows: BID/MBS/SSI 08-17, VIX 08-20); (2) MBB (ratio 0.1+0.15) and SSI (DIV value_per_share=1000, ISS ratio 0.2) corporate_action rows match the cited G5 formula inputs; (3) VHM ticker.Price stuck at 153,000 across 08-04/05/06 while Close correctly moved — confirms the claimed 'Price lags one session on ex-date' trap; (4) bot_execute.py wiring confirmed: apply_exdate_gate at line 521, check_plan_funding at line 565 — gate genuinely precedes funding gate; (5) positions_raw() exists in brokers.py with un-aggregated per-lot semantics as described; (6) the raw artifact [REDACTED]ogs/dnse_raw_[REDACTED]14.jsonl genuinely shows BID lot 1826 @35,800 vs lot 1258 @38,850 at ts 19:10:23 — the G4 ground-truth case is real, not fabricated; (7) the self-reported sys.path defect in merge_park_orders.py._has_event_in_window and its fix (independent _WC_ROOT anchor at line 180-181) are both present in the code exactly as described."}, "independent_recompute": "Reran exdate_price_frame_selfcheck.py (53/53 PASS, TZ-invariant) and replay_plans_regression.py against live BigQuery (61/61 no-event plans clean, 4 exact event-touched plans) from scratch — both matched the claimed numbers precisely. Also reran a live BQ query independently reproducing the event_status 0-vs-5 trap and 11/19 scope-map selfchecks, all matching or passing.", "killer_objection": "G5's cross-check formula depends on RIGHTS_ISSUE_PRICE, a single hand-entered constant (MBB rights price = 10,000 VND) that cannot be independently verified from BigQuery — value_per_share is NULL for every ISS row by design, so this number's only validation is that it was reverse-engineered to match the user's observed DNSE app reference price. That's a disclosed, narrowly-scoped limitation (keyed by ticker+date, fails CLOSED — blocks the order — if a future rights issue isn't in the table), not a fabrication, but it means G5 is not a fully independent two-source check for rights-issue events specifically, only for cash-dividend/stock-bonus events where value_per_share/exercise_ratio come straight from the vendor table.", "recommended_reruns": ["Run the remaining 8/19 scope-map selfchecks not sampled in this review (discretionary_target_pct, loan_package_resolution, paper_main_window, quote_l2_logging, refresh_skip_participation, t2_settlement, and the remaining corp_action variant) before treating the full 19/19 claim as independently closed.", "On [REDACTED] (the next real GDKHQ session: BID/MBS/SSI/VIX), do a live paper/dry-run trace of apply_exdate_gate against the actual generated plan before enabling it for real capital, to catch any DNSE positions_raw() response shape the offline artifacts didn't cover.", "Document a repeatable process for adding future RIGHTS_ISSUE_PRICE entries (who confirms the number, against what source) so G5 doesn't become a silent maintenance gap as new rights issues occur."], "summary": "This finding holds up under attack. I did not just read the code and the cited scripts — I re-ran them myself from a clean shell, including sourcing BigQuery credentials and hitting the live corporate_action table, and every headline number matched exactly: 53/53 selfcheck PASS lines including the two reverse-engineered proof cases (BID's split-lot price artifact and the plan_main_[REDACTED] mispriced-plan case), 61/61 historical plans untouched by the gate with precisely the 4 event-touched plans the design doc predicted, and the corp_action_lib announced-vs-executed status trap reproduced live (0 rows vs 5 rows) exactly as claimed. I also independently confirmed the raw DNSE artifact underlying the G4 same-frame invariant is real (not synthesized), confirmed the gate's wiring position in bot_execute.py genuinely sits before the funding gate, and reran 11 of the 19 cross-scope selfchecks the commit claims are unaffected — all green. No look-ahead leakage, no overfit parameters, and the fix is genuinely execution-layer (not a return-enhancing claim), so OOS/capacity attacks don't apply. The one soft spot is that the G5 cross-check's rights-issue price constant is a manually-maintained, unverifiable-from-BQ single entry — a real but disclosed and fail-closed limitation, not a flaw in the reasoning. The finding's own claim that this has NOT yet been applied to any real plan is also independently supported: no trade_plans or execution logs were touched after the commit timestamp."}
kb/events_buffer.md:598:- [[REDACTED]1:24:52Z] Taylor/finding — corp-action-sanity-factor-run-level-regression: {"summary": "Added t_run_level_wiring() (checks R1-R8) to corp_action_daily_selfcheck.py, closing the gap quant-skeptic flagged: all 178 prior magnitude-gate checks (MG1-MG16) call sanity_flag/sanity_warns/_fmt_magnitude directly, never through run(), so deleting the mag=sanity_warns(...) wiring inside run() left every existing test green. New test calls run(dry_run=True, alert=False) end-to-end with every [REDACTED] dependency patched (BQ/_fetch/oshares_at/gate_selfcheck/gate_freshness/read_positions/triggered_today/upcoming_events/bus/notify/OUT_DIR/STATE_PATH), injects a synthetic ticker MAG diverging 3.001x vs its quarterly OShares (matching the dispatch example 1000->3001), and asserts: value stays 3001 unsuppressed (R2), sanity_warn attached in place (R3), snapshot magnitude_suspect/magnitude_suspect_held populated (R4/R5), the 0x1F4CF (ruler) label reaches the Discord-bound dry-run message (R6), no real invariant-violation (0x1F6A8) line leaks in (R7). R8 is the mutant proof: stubbing sanity_warns+sanity_warns_from_crosscheck to no-ops inside the SAME hermetic harness makes magnitude_suspect empty and the ruler label disappear, proving the test catches a cut wire.", "verification": "Also mutated the REAL corp_action_daily.py in place (mag = [] instead of the real 3-line wiring at line 1422), re-ran the full selfcheck: R3/R4/R5/R6 correctly FAILED (4/186) while the other 178 pre-existing checks + R1/R7/R8 stayed green -- exact confirmation of the gap. Reverted immediately (git diff clean, confirmed). Final selfcheck on restored [REDACTED] file: PASS 186/186.", "test_file": "mike/bin/corp_action_daily_selfcheck.py", "selfcheck": "PASS 186/186", "mutant_caught": true, "commit": "5d0e1ba64ba0fff37f0725151bb57e293ea2b7b2", "note_on_commit": "commit-collision gate blocked my own git commit while Wags_20260819_012007 was live in this shared working copy; b